laurel 2998: LAUREL UCACHE: EL0 cache maintenance by VA is trapped and done with a clean first, so a JIT's new code is what the core fetches (Scion 49759b2, patch 1511); both kernels. docs/laurel_sprout/ios26-userland.md "JIT code".

[V Scion S9] iOS's sys_icache_invalidate() is DSB, IC IVAU per line, DSB, ISB and no DC CVAU: Apple's cores have CTR_EL0.IDC. The Kryo 260
reads IDC 0: a core can fetch the stale bytes under a line of new code still dirty in its L1 data cache (WebContent: SIGSEGV at pc 0 at its
first style resolution, 218 times on the S9). SCTLR_EL1.UCI is cleared on every core as it starts and wakes; the trapped IC IVAU and DC ops
are done on the kernel's alias of the page with DC CVAC first. Self-check: on only with CTR_EL0.IDC 0. Kill switch laurelucache=0. One line.
iOS 26: the sleh.c and arm_init.c hunks are in post/9020 (the base owns those files; owned.txt lists 2998).

